WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.040
Is Jay-Z really in the Illuminati?

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.960
Is Donald Trump? Is Katy Perry?

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:07.920
Am I?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.560
Everyone from the BBC to Beyoncé

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.640
has been accused of
being part of the Illuminati -

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.960
a secret group said to comprise of
the world's most powerful people

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.200
seeking to establish
a new world order.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.600
Even if you haven't
heard of the Illuminati,

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.680
chances are you've probably seen one
of the symbols associated with them.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.800
Pentagrams, goats,

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.160
even the all-seeing eye
that's found on US banknotes.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.200
References have also cropped up
in music videos,

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.960
such as Rihanna's S&amp;M,

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.600
which featured a fake newspaper
with a headline declaring her...

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.320
So why do musicians and artists

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.880
like to play around
with references to the Illuminati?

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.600
I think quite simply,
they're just having fun.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.200
They're just entertained by these
stories like many of us are.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.240
I'm reminded of a conspiracy
theory from 1966

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.320
that Paul McCartney of The Beatles
had died in a car crash

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.280
on the way home after
doing some recording

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:07.320
and he'd been replaced
by a Canadian DJ

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.080
who looked a lot like him and quickly
learned to play the bass and sing.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.080
Paul McCartney has never denied
this conspiracy theory.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.520
He's always kept quiet about it

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:20.720
and I think McCartney,
like Jay-Z, Rihanna and others,

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.560
is just entertained by the story.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.720
So who are the Illuminati?

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.280
Are they really a shadowy elite
who control the world?

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.320
The Illuminati were,
to the best of our knowledge,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.240
a Bavarian secret society
formed in the 18th Century.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.880
It opposed superstition, religious
influence and state authority.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.960
They even created a rule book
which stated that...

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.160
The Bavarian group
eventually faded into irrelevance

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.720
and has nothing to do with modern
concepts of the Illuminati.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.200
The conspiracy theory
that we know about today

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.480
stems from the Discordian movement.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.800
The story goes that
Discordianism began in 1965

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.440
in the office of
a Texas drug attorney.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.000
Two schoolmates...

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.360
...used the office photocopier
to publish copies

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:18.880
of the Principia Discordia,
the movement's founding text.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.640
The book promoted the idea that...

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.520
...and Discordianism gathered steam
throughout the 60s and 70s

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.520
with Hill and Thornley
actively trying

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.040
to cause mischief
and spread disinformation.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.760
Their mission was expanded even
further by two other Americans -

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.520
a writer called Robert Anton Wilson
and his friend Robert Shea.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.480
Wilson was editor at Playboy

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.200
and the two of them decided
they would write a novel

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:47.640
and they would throw all of the great
conspiracy theories into this novel

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.240
and call it Illuminatus.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.720
And in fact, they enjoyed it so much
they turned it into a trilogy.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:57.040
They decided that it would
be fun to try and spread

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.000
a little chaos and misinformation
deliberately about the Illuminati

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.560
and they did this by writing letters
to the mainstream press,

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.960
by writing letters to fanzines -
which were popular at the time -

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.240
but also through the
letters page of Playboy itself.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.400
They would also write in letters
from imaginary readers

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.960
saying that the Illuminati
weren't real at all

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.480
or were kind of sitting on the fence.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.160
It didn't really matter, what did
matter is that all these people

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:28.280
seemed to be generating this
conversation about the Illuminati.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.720
And the idea was that you,
as the reader,

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.480
were supposed to question that,

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:36.040
interrogate it, ask,
"Are they really real?"

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.240
The myth travelled far and wide.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.960
Wilson and Shea's
The Illuminatus Trilogy

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.240
attributed some of the
mysteries of the time,

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:47.000
such as, "Who shot John F. Kennedy?"
to the Illuminati.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.600
Although the multitude
of conspiracy theories

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:52.120
that appear in the trilogy
are imaginary,

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.080
they're blended with enough truth
to make them seem plausible.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.600
Probably the oddest theory
was the suggestion that

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.200
Adam Weishaupt, the founder
of the Bavarian Illuminati,

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:07.040
assassinated George Washington
and assumed his identity

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.880
{as President of the USA.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.960
Believers of this theory
point to Washington's portrait

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.400
on the US one dollar bill

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.040
which they suggest
is actually the face of Weishaupt.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:21.240
Despite its lack of mainstream sales
the trilogy became a cult favourite.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.480
It was even made into a mammoth
eight-hour stage play in Liverpool,

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.440
launching the careers of British
actors Bill Nighy and Jim Broadbent.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.920
The 70s print magazine culture
seems distant now

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.640
from our globalised
hyper-connected internet,

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:40.200
but Illuminati rumours are still rife
on websites such as 4chan and Reddit

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:43.280
where believers swap their favourite
versions of the conspiracy

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:46.960
and champion evidence
to prove it's still in existence.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.640
Ultimately it's not down to a shadowy
elite whether you choose to believe

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.760
in the Illuminati
conspiracy theory or not.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.200
It's up to you.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.100
Thanks for watching. Don't forget to subscribe

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.880
and click the bell to receive notifications for new videos.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.880
See you again soon!

